joining us once again on the program the  armed forces minister james heapey  minister always good to have you on the  programme and as always lots for us to  discuss so let's let let's start shall  we with the kind of the overview of  where the conflict is currently the dod  and the mod seem to be an agreement that  the russians have made precious little  advance over the past week but i'm  wondering whether or not you are  concerned about what we've just seen in  the past few years in la viv what  appears to be the use of cruise missiles  to take out part of the airport facility  yeah i mean i think that's exactly right  niall that on the sort of macro level  when you look at the whole map the  russians are making very very little  progress and yet they continue to expend  a significant amount of military  resource  and  that is great credit to the resistance  the ukrainians are putting up  but on the sort of on the the sort of  smaller more local level what's going on  in mario paul is a cause for huge  concern the city is uh under a level of  barrage that is utterly terrifying and  disastrous for the population that  remains there the ukrainian mps that  visited me here in the ministry of  defence yesterday uh were telling me  that maybe 90 of the city is is now  being uh affected um and as you say you  know the there are now two strikes into  western ukraine the air base last week  and uh and strikes nov last night um so  whilst there's no macro progress  we're very concerned about the suffering  of the people in mario paul and other  cities that are under siege in the east  and the fact that ukrainian supply lines  are starting to be attacked in the west  it it certainly looks that there has  been a tactic of blanket bombardment  when it comes to mario paul in terms of  the russian strategy there you'll have  heard just in the past couple of minutes  though  in martha's report the russian  ambassador to to the united nations  denying any russian involvement in what  happened in that theater in mario paul  what is our intelligence telling us  about responsibility  i don't know how the russian ambassador  sleeps at night because you know he sits  there he stands there and he says that  to your correspondent that it is  it is clear as day what's happening in  in mario the russians are  indiscriminately  using uh artillery and missile strikes  to  um to destroy a city that they were  unable to take militarily and the  resistance that remains in there is  courageous the problem is is that mario  paul is probably the worst it's the one  that we're most concerned about but  actually um there's not dissimilar  things happening in kharkiv  as well and other faces besides um this  is a barbaric tactic the russians have  failed to do this militarily they  thought that they could do it in days  and what it looks like they're going to  try to do is to encircle these cities  and just then use artillery uh and  missile strikes in order to  to um to force the ukrainians into  submission but the ukrainians so no sign  of doing that and that's to their  enormous credit  um mr [ __ ] you and i have spoken enough  uh enough times that i know that you  choose your words very carefully so just  to pick you up in some of the things  that you said there barbaric tactics you  know it's clear as day what the russians  are doing there how does the russian  ambassador to the u.n sleep at night is  this now not the point for us to do what  the american president has done  and call vladimir putin what he  apparently is a war criminal a murderous  dictator a pure thug  well i mean i've  not pulled my punches when i've been on  your um on your show previously and i  think that the evidence that is  uh that is being gathered points very  much towards uh war crimes being  committed in ukraine and the culpability  for war crimes sits absolutely with the  leader of the russian government the man  who decided to do all of this in the  first place but the other point to make  and it's an important point to make is  that it's not just putin who ends up  being responsible for war crimes as and  when the evidence is gathered and people  are held to account every single person  in the military of chain of command  cannot just hide behind the line of  their only following orders they too are  involved in the prosecution of war  crimes in ukraine this is uh a stay  on uh on the russian nation and i know  because i can i see information about  some of the questions that russians are  asking on on on search platforms um you  know russians are  questioning whether or not the behavior  of their president and their armed  forces um is quite how it's being  presented to them on the russian media  and the answer is it's not their russia  the russian armed forces are letting the  russian people down their president is  letting the russian people down  given what we we've seen in mario paul  and indeed as you mentioned in a lot of  other places around ukraine it does  perhaps feel like we're putting the cat  before the horse but people are  beginning to talk about  how the conflict may well come to an end  and discussions seem to be in part  centering around the west you know the  united kingdom france the americans and  others somehow guaranteeing ukraine's  safety in the future i mean isn't that  just nato membership by another name  i don't think so i mean i think that  we've got to be we've got to be clear  that this  can't go on indefinitely that the thing  that all of us want  is not the the the endless arming of the  ukrainians so that they can resist as  necessary as that is for as long as the  fighting continues we don't want the  ukrainians to uh have to lose or to give  up their country but what we do need  clearly is a situation in which the two  sides meet and come to some sort of  arrangement if the west has a role to  play alongside others beyond the region  in brokering that piece and  offering something that uh that 